  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: both routes. Fail closed. All of these REFUSE and execute nothing: a missing bearer token, an OBO exchange failure, a WhoAmI failure, `GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` returning null or `Guid.Empty`, the SDK entry point refusing, and Dataverse refusing impersonation. There is NO app-only fallback and NO retry as the app on any path of either route. Unknown and denied ids answer the same on the record route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: identity. The impersonated identity is the systemuserid returned by `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync(TokenHelper.ExtractBearerTokenOrNull(httpContext), ct)`, resolved in the HANDLER of each route, after the existing request validation and before any service call (the precedent at `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:719-722`). Do not add an oid → systemuserid lookup, and do not use `UserPrivilegeChecker`'s private lookup, `ISystemUserIdentityResolver` or `ICallerSystemUserResolver` for this. Do not take any identity from the request body, query, route or any request header other than the validated bearer token.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: impersonation mechanism. Add exactly ONE public SDK entry point to `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs`, for example `ServiceClient CloneAsSystemUser(ServiceClient appClient, Guid systemUserId)`. It checks `systemUserId == Guid.Empty` FIRST and throws `ArgumentException` (ParamName `systemUserId`) before touching `appClient`, so the refusal is testable with no live client. It then null-checks `appClient`, calls `appClient.Clone()`, sets `CallerId = systemUserId` on the CLONE, and returns the clone; the caller disposes it. A clone that is null or not `IsReady` is disposed and refused with `InvalidOperationException`. NEVER set `CallerId` or `CallerAADObjectId` on the singleton ServiceClient: that would leak one caller's identity into concurrent requests. `UserPrivilegeChecker.cs:147-148` switches to this entry point (behaviour identical: its systemuserid is already non-empty at that point, and its surrounding try/catch still fails closed to an empty set), so `src/server` has exactly one place that assigns an impersonation identity on an SDK client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: FetchService and RecordService. Add `ExecuteAsCallerAsync(FetchRequestDto request, Guid callerSystemUserId, CancellationToken ct)` and `GetRecordAsCallerAsync(string entityLogicalName, Guid id, string[]? selectFields, Guid callerSystemUserId, CancellationToken ct)`. The names are deliberately NOT overloads of `ExecuteAsync` / `GetRecordAsync`, so the method-group conversions at `ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs:189` and `:320` stay unambiguous. They run the SAME FetchXML / paging-cookie / projection code as the app-only methods (extract shared private helpers if needed, without changing the app-only methods' observable behaviour), on the clone from the new entry point, disposed in a `finally`. The app-only `ExecuteAsync` and `GetRecordAsync` keep their signatures and behaviour byte-identical. To make the real host testable, the two classes may be unsealed and ONLY the two new methods made `virtual` (the task-130 precedent: "FinanceRollupService entry points made virtual"). `RecordService.ResolveDefaultColumnsAsync` may keep reading entity METADATA app-only (schema, not record data).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: fault classification. Add ONE `internal static` classifier (`Services/Dataverse/DataverseCallerFaultClassifier.cs`) that classifies an exception from the impersonated call by Dataverse error code, never by message text, into exactly four outcomes: NotFound, AccessDenied, ImpersonationRefused, Other. NotFound is decided by calling the existing `RecordContainerResolver.IsRecordNotFound(Exception)` (do not copy the 0x80040217 constant). AccessDenied = `OrganizationServiceFault.ErrorCode` -2147187962 (0x80048306) or -2147220960 (0x80040220), plus any further code the live gate shows for an unreadable row (recorded in the note). ImpersonationRefused = 0x8004A110. The classifier finds the `FaultException&lt;OrganizationServiceFault&gt;` at the top level or anywhere in the `InnerException` chain; if Step 0 or the live gate shows the cloned ServiceClient surfaces these faults as a different exception type that carries the code, the classifier reads that type too (recorded in the note). It is testable with constructed `FaultException&lt;OrganizationServiceFault&gt;` instances (ADR-038 B8 permits internal + InternalsVisibleTo).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: route responses — a closed set.
• fetch: identity null → 403, errorCode `DV_CALLER_NOT_RESOLVED`; AccessDenied → 403, errorCode `DV_PRIVILEGE_DENIED`, title "Forbidden", the same extension keys (`errorCode`, `correlationId`) as `DataverseAuthorizationFilter.DataverseProblem` (`DataverseAuthorizationFilter.cs:281-296`), and ONE constant detail that does not echo the fault message (a Dataverse privilege fault message names the principal's systemuserid and role counts); ImpersonationRefused, the entry point throwing, or Other → 500 errorCode `DV_IMPERSONATION_UNAVAILABLE` for the first two and the existing `DV_FETCH_INTERNAL_ERROR` for Other, never echoing the message.
• record: identity null, NotFound and AccessDenied → ONE uniform 404: status 404, title "Not Found", ONE constant detail string that contains neither the id nor the entity name, errorCode `DV_RECORD_NOT_FOUND`, and the same extension keys (`errorCode`, `correlationId`). Every `RecordNotFoundException` this route returns (including the `ResolveDefaultColumnsAsync` unknown-entity path) uses that same body. ImpersonationRefused or the entry point throwing → 500 `DV_IMPERSONATION_UNAVAILABLE`; Other → the existing 500 `DV_RECORD_INTERNAL_ERROR`.
• ORDERING (record route): the record handler's existing `catch (ArgumentException)` (`RecordEndpoints.cs:119-133`) and `IsInvalidSelectField` heuristic (`:139-155`) both ECHO `ex.Message` as a 400. They must never see the entry point's `ArgumentException` refusal or a NotFound / AccessDenied / ImpersonationRefused fault: those are classified and mapped FIRST, whatever the mechanism (classified in the as-caller method, or caught before those catches in the handler).
Every other existing response (401, 400 validation, 400 malformed FetchXML, 400 entity mismatch, 400 invalid $select for a genuinely unknown column, the filter's entity-level 403) is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DataverseAuthorizationFilter. Keep it attached to both routes and do not change its behaviour. It still gives the cheap, documented entity-level 403 that BffDataverseClient maps, and the savedquery, metadata and gridconfigurations routes in `Api/Dataverse/` use it too. Correct only its misleading doc comment (`:29-32`). Do not change `IDataversePrivilegeChecker` / `UserPrivilegeChecker` semantics beyond the two-line clone change (`Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryAccessAuthorizer.cs`, registered at `Infrastructure/DI/AiPersistenceModule.cs:154-157`, also consumes the checker).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the external module seam. `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs` is NOT modified by this task, and its tests pass unmodified. A contact cannot be impersonated (project CLAUDE.md fact 4); that seam's app-only reads are scoped by Tier-2 injection and the column allow-list (tasks 134/157).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: response shape. Both routes return exactly the JSON shape they return today for an authorized caller (the FetchService `ProjectEntity` and RecordService `ProjectEntityToDictionary` projections). The only permitted differences are the ones Dataverse itself makes for the caller: fewer rows, and field-level-secured columns absent or null where the caller lacks field read. Do not move these routes to the Web API (`RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync`) or to `IDataverseUserClient`; both change the shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the route guard (task 167). Before editing `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs`, check whether task 167 has landed on this branch: `GovernedFiles` contains `Api/Dataverse/FetchEndpoints.cs` / `RecordEndpoints.cs`, and the guard governs every route file.
• If 167 HAS landed: DELETE every Pending waiver 167 added for `POST /api/dataverse/fetch` and `GET /api/dataverse/record/{entityLogicalName}/{id:guid}`. If 167 recorded these routes some other way (because `FilterMarker` already reads them as gated), follow 167's documented mechanism for "the impersonated execution is the gate" and update only the entries for these two routes. Edit the reason text of the `Api/Dataverse/FetchEndpoints.cs` / `RecordEndpoints.cs` GovernedFile entries (if 167 created them) to say: DataverseAuthorizationFilter is entity-level only; the per-resource decision is the impersonated execution (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` + `DataverseImpersonation`), pinned by `DataverseImpersonationSiteGuardTests` rule 2. Do NOT add a Permanent waiver only to annotate a route the guard already reads as gated (maintenance rule 4). `NoWaiverIsStale`, Rule A, Rule B and the census stay green.
• If 167 has NOT landed: do NOT edit `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs`. Record in the task note the exact entries the guard needs for these two routes (the GovernedFile classification and reason text above, and the fact that FilterMarker credits `.AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(` so no Pending waiver is possible), so the main session reconciles them at integration.
In both cases, do not change `FilterMarker`, `DecisionServices` or `ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames` (guard design belongs to task 167; see escalation trigger 3).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">No Dataverse plugins. Row security comes from Dataverse evaluating the impersonated call; nothing is added on the Dataverse side.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no `Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests, no reflection into non-public members. Substitute at the existing seams: a `CallerRecordAccessProbe` subclass overriding `GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` (the `DelegationRuleTestFixture.cs:219` pattern, registered as `CallerRecordAccessProbe`); FetchService/RecordService subclasses overriding only the two new virtual methods, registered in `DataverseIntegrationTestFixture`; constructed `FaultException&lt;OrganizationServiceFault&gt;` instances for the classifier and for the subclasses to throw. Drive the REAL host and the REAL `MapFetchEndpoints` / `MapRecordEndpoints`. No live Dataverse in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: bite proofs. Every new guard is proven to bite by seeding its removal, running the named test, watching it FAIL, and restoring. Record each proof in the task note: the seeded change, the failing test, and its failure message.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (hard gate)">Scope: before the PR. Run `dotnet test` on the affected projects, then the FULL BFF unit suite (`tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests`), `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests`, and BOTH integration suites in full: `tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` and `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests`. A build alone is not a run. Also run the `Spaarke.UI.Components` test for `BffDataverseClient.test.ts` (it must pass unchanged).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`: in BFF; existing routes; no new service, filter, map or OperationAccessPolicy key; one helper entry point in Spaarke.Dataverse; one internal static fault classifier (three-question justification in the PR). Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master and a FRESH build of the branch, both from SHORT paths, both zipped with Compress-Archive (the `scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1` method), with equal file counts. Report both absolute sizes, the delta and the zip tool; the ceiling is 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 / round 9 (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred: scope discovered during execution is added here. Live Dataverse is READ-ONLY during development; the live gate is run by the main session. Do not relocate or re-role users. For a user at a specific access level, ask the owner rather than reusing the root-BU dev users (round 4 item 1, round 5 item 1).</constraint>
  </constraints>

