  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/dataverse/fetch executes as the caller. Through the real host, the FetchService caller-scoped method receives exactly the systemuserid the (stubbed) `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerSystemUserIdAsync` returned for that request's bearer token, and the 200 body is the stub's rows projected as today. The app-only `FetchService.ExecuteAsync` is not called by this route (proven by arch guard rule 2 and bite proof (a)).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/dataverse/fetch, negative (caller identity not proven): when the probe returns null (covers no bearer token, OBO failure, WhoAmI failure, and a caller with no systemuser such as a contact) or `Guid.Empty`, the route returns 403 with errorCode `DV_CALLER_NOT_RESOLVED`, and NEITHER FetchService method is invoked. With the fixture's REAL probe (no OBO configuration) the route also refuses this way.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/dataverse/fetch, negative (no rights on the rows): the response carries exactly the rows the caller-scoped execution returned, with no rows added and no app-only re-query. An AccessDenied fault (each of 0x80048306 and 0x80040220, two cases) from the impersonated execution returns 403 `DV_PRIVILEGE_DENIED` with title "Forbidden", the `errorCode` and `correlationId` extension keys, and a constant detail that contains no part of the fault message (asserted by seeding the fault message with a marker GUID and asserting the body does not contain it).</criterion>
